INT. ROLLER DERBY LOCKER ROOM - NIGHT

Concrete floor. Steel lockers, dented. Fluorescent flicker. A hundred pairs of skates on hooks. The scoreboard through the wall reads 142-38.

COACH BERNADETTE "BERNIE" OYELOWO, 50s, in a tracksuit and whistle, stands in the centre with a dry-erase marker. Her jaw is clamped.

SUNNIVA HOLM, 20s, jammer, the team's star, sits on a bench with her helmet in her lap. Her lip is split.

TILLY BRANDT, 20s, blocker, ponytail, holds an ice pack to her wrist.

MARGOT "TANK" DELACROIX, 30s, enormous, sits on the floor tying a skate.

RAJANI PILLAI, 20s, rookie, stands against the wall, wide-eyed.

DIEDRE KOWALCZYK, 30s, captain, rubs her knuckles raw with a towel.

BERNIE
Final period. One hundred and four points down.

SUNNIVA
I know.

BERNIE
I didn't ask if you knew.

TANK
Coach, with respect, we're being killed.

BERNIE
Then die loud.

DIEDRE
We can't win.

BERNIE
You can't win. You can lose with dignity.

TILLY
That doesn't sound like a pep talk.

BERNIE
It isn't. It's the truth.

RAJANI
(small voice)
Can I say something?

BERNIE
Please.

RAJANI
This is the best night of my life.

Silence. The lockers hum.

TANK
She's serious.

RAJANI
I've watched you play since I was twelve. Now I'm in the locker room. We're losing a hundred and four to thirty-eight, and I'm so happy I could throw up.

SUNNIVA
(laughing)
Rookie.

DIEDRE
Welcome to the team.

Tilly tosses her ice pack across the room. Tank catches it, flings it back. Sunniva swats it out of the air, knocks Rajani's helmet off her head. Rajani lunges for it; Diedre grabs the helmet, stuffs it on Tank's head. They collapse into a wrestling pile of limbs and laughter. Bernie lets them for a full five seconds. Then she blows her whistle.

BERNIE
Go skate.

They file out. Bernie caps the marker. Waits until the room is empty.

BERNIE (CONT'D)
(to herself)
Dignity.
